# Ilyrium control-panel — environment template (NO secrets in git; copy to .env and fill).
#
# ── DB TOPOLOGY + WHICH CONNECTION STRING TO USE → docs/relay/NEON_TOPOLOGY.md ──
# Three Neon projects all read like "ilyrium". Identify by PROJECT ID + db CONTENTS, never by
# display name. The real studio DB is project `patient-star-32154915` (display name "studio-os")
# / database `ilyrium`. `ep-…` endpoint ids DRIFT; `br-…`/project ids are STABLE.
#
# DATABASE_URL — the studio `ilyrium` DB (project patient-star-32154915):
#   • Prisma CLI / DDL / Phase-2 Graphile Worker → DIRECT (non-`-pooler`) host; DROP channel_binding.
#   • Vercel / serverless runtime               → POOLED (`-pooler`) host.
#   • path must be /ilyrium (NEVER /neondb — a wrong db connects and shows Campaign/Scene).
#   • Pull the real string from the Neon console / Vercel env. Never commit a password.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://neondb_owner:<password>@ep-<endpoint>.c-7.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/ilyrium?sslmode=require

# Trap: a shell `DATABASE_URL` overrides this file under dotenv. `unset DATABASE_URL` (and
# `NODE_ENV`) before prisma/build if you launched from another project (e.g. PermitHub).

# ── fal.ai media generation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FAL_KEY: server-only fal.ai API key (never use NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix).
# Generate at: https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys
# FAL_KEY=key_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# FAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET: used to verify x-fal-signature HMAC-SHA256 on incoming webhooks.
# Set this in the fal.ai dashboard under Webhooks → Secret.
# FAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADAPTER: set to "fal" to route video/image generation through fal.ai
# (falVideoAdapter + falImageAdapter are prepended in adapter-bus).
# Leave unset to fall back to mock placeholder adapters.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADAPTER=fal

# Optional: override per-second cost estimates (defaults: 40 for video, 5 for image).
# FAL_CENTS_PER_SEC_VIDEO=40
# FAL_CENTS_PER_SEC_IMAGE=5
